  "final_text": "I generated `input_eta_costheta_scan.dat` for the \u03b7-channel scan (W=1.7 GeV, Q\u00b2=1.5 GeV\u00b2, \u03c6*=90\u00b0) at 5 cos \u03b8* points. Both kinematic points are physical \u2014 W=1.7 GeV is well above the \u03b7 threshold (1.4856 GeV) and within the EtaMAID table grid, and Q\u00b2=1.5 GeV\u00b2 is in range.\n\nOne fix applied: a literal linspace(-1, 1) puts endpoints exactly at cos \u03b8*=\u00b11 (\u03b8*=0\u00b0/180\u00b0), where the exact bremsstrahlung phase-space integral has a vanishing Jacobian and is known to trigger the NAG `d01fce` integration failure referenced in the input template. The repo's own multi-point example avoids this by using \u00b10.999 instead of \u00b11, so I did the same \u2014 endpoints are now -0.999/+0.999, interior points (-0.5, 0, 0.5) unchanged. Details are in `outcome.json`."
